course: dictionary
lesson: 15235
title: Sharer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sharer is a person who shares something with other people. To share means to let others have a part of what you have, so they can use it too. The ending -er often means a person who does something, so a sharer is one who shares.
explain: «Mia is a good sharer. She lets her friends paint with her brushes.» The sentence shows what a sharer does: Mia gives other children a turn with her things.
explain: A sharer can also be someone who shares a flat or house with other people. In the UK this is called a house sharer. «Sam is a flat sharer, and he and his friends split the bills.» Read the words around sharer to find which meaning fits.
fact: A sharer is a person who shares something with others.
fact: «A good sharer» is a child who shares toys and games kindly.
fact: A flat sharer, or in the UK a house sharer, is someone who shares a flat or house with other people.
fact: In maths, sharers are the people who split a total equally: «Four sharers split 12 sweets, so each gets 3.»
exercise: «Ella is a good sharer. She lets everyone have a turn on the swing.» What is a sharer? | A swing in the park | A person who is always late | *A person who shares something with others | A person who keeps everything just for themselves
exercise: «Six sharers split 18 stickers equally.» How many stickers does each sharer get? | 2 | 12 | *3 | 6
exercise: Tom and Raj are flat sharers in the same city. What does flat sharer mean? | Someone who cleans windows | Someone who lives alone in a castle | Someone who sells flats | *Someone who shares a flat with other people
test: Which phrase means a child who shares toys kindly? | *a good sharer | A fast runner | A sad sleeper | A loud shouter
test: «Four sharers divide 20 marbles equally.» How many marbles does each sharer get? | 24 | 4 | 16 | *5
exam: Which sentence uses sharer correctly? | «The sharers of the sun were very hot.» | *«Our house has three sharers, and we all share the bills.» | «I sharer my lunch with my friend on Monday.» | «The sharer barked loudly at the postman.»
